  'Captain Johannes Glen built this house in 1713, partly of materials from the first house in the Mohawk Valley, which Alexander Glen built in 1655 (1932 state marker). The family held it for more than two centuries; it became an inn in the 1960s and grew into a wedding and dining venue of over 40,000 square feet with a ballroom and 22 guest rooms. A 2026 report says the catering business was sold to Compass International and the real estate was put on the market.',
